      {
        "id": 152633,
        "name": "lynkfox",
        "username": "lynkfox",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-14T00:40:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"waedens\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/w/b3f665/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> waedens:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My copy has been bouncing around Atlanta (where I live) since Friday. It has never been more than a 20 or 30 minute drive away from me. I would have gladly drove over and picked it up. As it is the schedule says it will be delivered on Wednesday. I think they have opened it up and are getting in a few games before they deliver it to me.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Waedens, you can actually do that. Call the number I listed above, (1800gofedex) and if it hasn't gone out on a truck, you can usually go down to the terminal and pick it up. Just bring your tracking number and an ID with your address on it.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
